              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 3,
                "start": 3
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "The petitioner argues that, although the FCC has ample authority to enforce the compensation system, violations of its regulations do not give rise to a private cause of action under sections\u202f206 and\u202f207 of the Communications Act, and nothing in \u00a7276 contemplates such a private right of action."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Fisher",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "3d56503e761ffbe33dd5b3468ca347f6224832465796411c3d7b72009f31377f",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-3d56503e761f-0001-0002"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 25,
                "start": 25
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Fisher, the petitioner contends that the FCC\u2019s authority derives from Section\u202f154(i) and other provisions, allowing it to craft enforcement regimes, but not to create private rights of action."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Jeffrey L. Fisher",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "3d56503e761ffbe33dd5b3468ca347f6224832465796411c3d7b72009f31377f",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-3d56503e761f-0002-0007"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 52,
                "start": 52
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Jeffrey L. Fisher, the petitioner maintains that the matter is not a covered practice; the FCC\u2019s authority extends to carrier\u2011customer relationships, not carrier\u2011supplier relationships."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Global Crossing",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "3d56503e761ffbe33dd5b3468ca347f6224832465796411c3d7b72009f31377f",
              "evidence_ids": [
